NETCTL(2)                      P32W Unix                       NETCTL(2)

NAME
       netctl - the network interface and host names

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/netctl.h>

       int netctl(int cmd, void *arg);

DESCRIPTION
       P32W's own call for the network coprocessor's settings.

       NETCTL_INFO fills a struct netinfo: flags (NETF_UP, the link
       is up; NETF_ADDR, an address is set; NETF_DHCP, by DHCP),
       the MAC address, and the address, netmask, gateway and DNS
       server, in network byte order.

       NETCTL_CONFIG (root only) sets them from a struct netconfig:
       dhcp non-zero to get them by DHCP, else the four addresses.

       NETCTL_RESOLVE looks up the host name in a struct
       netresolve's name, through the DNS server, and puts its
       address in addr. gethostbyname(3) uses it.

RETURN VALUE
       0; -1 on an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENETDOWN  No coprocessor.
       ENOENT    NETCTL_RESOLVE: no such host.
       ENOBUFS   No coprocessor socket free for the lookup.
       EPERM     NETCTL_CONFIG, and not root.
       EINVAL    An unknown cmd.

SEE ALSO
       socket(2), inet(3)
